;; arm64 makes an add of a compare's 0 or 1 as the compare and a cinc of
;; the other operand (isel.c find_cincs), where cset made the 0 or 1 and
;; an add added it: every integer compare and eqz, its right operand a
;; register, an immediate, a negative one, a constant no immediate takes
;; and a constant on the left; both orders of the add; an i64's add of the
;; compare's extension; float compares, NaN among their operands; a count
;; carried round a loop; and the near misses that keep their csets.
;; Made by test/gen_cinc.py, which works out every answer.
